  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "Eliphaz counsels Job: Man is born unto trouble, seek unto God, and happy is the man whom God corrects.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Call now, if there be any that will answer thee; and to which of the saints wilt thou turn?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "HEB holy ones."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For wrath killeth the foolish man, and envy slayeth the silly one.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "OR naive."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "I have seen the foolish taking root: but suddenly I cursed his habitation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "His children are far from safety, and they are crushed in the gate, neither is there any to deliver them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 84
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose harvest the hungry eateth up, and taketh it even out of the thorns, and the robber swalloweth up their substance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Although affliction cometh not forth of the dust, neither doth trouble spring out of the ground;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet man is born unto trouble, as the sparks fly upward.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Adversity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Adversity.",
            "prettyString": "TG Adversity",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Adversity",
                "entryId": "tg-adversity",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "I would seek unto God, and unto God would I commit my cause:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Which doeth great things and unsearchable; marvellous things without number:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Who giveth rain upon the earth, and sendeth waters upon the fields:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "To set up on high those that be low; that those which mourn may be exalted to safety.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Mourning.",
            "prettyString": "TG Mourning",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Mourning",
                "entryId": "tg-mourning",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "He disappointeth the devices of the crafty, so that their hands cannot perform their enterprise.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "He taketh the wise in their own craftiness: and the counsel of the froward is carried headlong.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "They meet with darkness in the daytime, and grope in the noonday as in the night.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "But he saveth the poor from the sword, from their mouth, and from the hand of the mighty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "So the poor hath hope, and iniquity stoppeth her mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, happy is the man whom God correcteth: therefore despise not thou the chastening of the Almighty:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Happiness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Happiness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Happiness",
                "entryId": "tg-happiness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Chastening.",
            "prettyString": "TG Chastening",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Chastening",
                "entryId": "tg-chastening",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "For he maketh sore, and bindeth up: he woundeth, and his hands make whole.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "HEB smites, bruises."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall deliver thee in six troubles: yea, in seven there shall no evil touch thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "In famine he shall redeem thee from death: and in war from the power of the sword.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 5:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt be hid from the scourge of the tongue: neither shalt thou be afraid of destruction when it cometh.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "D&C 38:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 38:30.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 38:30",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 38,
                    "end": 38,
